      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "For a survey, a sample of 1,018 people was selected at random from all registered voters in a\ncounty. Based on the survey, it is estimated that $66 \\%$ of all registered voters in the county are\nin favor of a new law, with an associated margin of error of $2.91 \\%$ . Which of the following\nbest describes the plausible values for the percent of all registered voters in the county who are in\nfavor of the new law?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-ad2e25df47df4a2283d42573d8f62e64",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m2-q4"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Any value greater than $63.09 \\%$ and less than $68.91 \\%$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Any value greater than $63.09 \\%$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Any value less than $63.09 \\%$ or greater than $68.91 \\%$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Any value less than $68.91 \\%$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
